  "equipment_type": "Duct / outdoor sensors (temperature, humidity, CO2, VOC, differential pressure)",
  "applies_to": "Belimo BACnet MS/TP sensors: 22DTH duct temperature/humidity, 22UTH outdoor temperature/humidity, 22DTM duct CO2/VOC and 22ADP differential pressure/airflow sensors.",
  "summary": "This family of Belimo sensors shares one BACnet MS/TP object map. AI 0-11 carry the measured values (temperature, humidity, derived absolute humidity, enthalpy and dew point, CO2, VOC, differential pressure and fan airflow), and AV objects hold offsets, output scaling limits, channel assignment, fan k-factors, device settings and the optional LCD. Only the values the particular model measures are in service; the rest show Out of Service.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": "2.3",
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "The document gives no BACnet object names, only instances and descriptions; names here are the printed descriptions.",
    "Points not measured by a given model read Out of Service; check the datasheet for which apply.",
    "SI or Imperial units are chosen with AV 38; on 22ADP models DIP switch 6 sets this instead.",
    "AV 22-25 are printed as AI[22]-AI[25] in the document but sit in the AV limits table and are R/W.",
    "AV 50 appears twice in the document (deduplicated); AV 56 and AV 57 share the same text.",
    "Document cover says Edition 2024-03 / V4.2 although the file name says V4_1."
  ],
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Set the MS/TP MAC address and baud rate on the RS-485 module's DIP switches, then read the AI objects the model supports. Offsets, limits and the SI/Imperial choice are configuration AVs to set once. For 22ADP fan airflow, set the fan manufacturer and k-factor first.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "AI 0",
        "name": "Value temperature",
        "why": "Temperature (22DTH / 22UTH / 22DTM)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 1",
        "name": "Value relative humidity",
        "why": "Relative humidity (22DTH / 22UTH)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 5",
        "name": "Value CO2",
        "why": "CO2 (22DTM)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 8",
        "name": "Differential pressure 1",
        "why": "Differential pressure (22ADP)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 9",
        "name": "Volumetric flow 1",
        "why": "Fan airflow (22ADP)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 4",
        "name": "Value dew point",
        "why": "Dew point"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 38",
        "name": "Selection of the unitary system",
        "why": "SI or Imperial units"
      }
    ],
    "enable": null,
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "MS/TP only; MAC address 1-127 set in binary on DIP1 switches 1-5 plus DIP2 switches 4-5 (0 is reserved).",
      "Baud rate on DIP2 switches 2-3: 9600, 19200, 38400 or 76800.",
      "DIP2 switch 1 turns on the 120 Ω terminator; all DIP switches ship OFF.",
      "Device ID = AV 46 offset + MAC address.",
      "Unconfirmed COV (AV 47) is the COV method; there are no COV subscriptions (DS-COVU-B only)."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "inWC offsets in AV 4/5 are written in thousandths (write 10 for 0.01 inWC).",
      "AV 39 altitude is always entered in metres.",
      "The 22ADP differential pressure range is set by DIP switches 1-3 on the sensor main board.",
      "Channel numbers 1 and 2 also drive the two 0-10 V outputs AOU1/AOU2."
    ]
  },
